ery the book published  today is option B facing adversity  building resilience and finding joy  written with psychologist Adam grant and  how do you develop resilience we develop  resilience by believing  that we will get through hard things we  grow stronger by living through horrible  moments or real adversity I never  thought I would live through some of  those unimaginable moments but I have  grown stronger my kids have perspective  I would never wish on them but it is  perspective  my son's basketball team lost the  playoffs a few weeks ago and all the  other kids were really upset and I said  are you okay and he looked at me and  said mom this is sixth-grade basketball  I'm fine well I'm fine yeah the book  option B is on sale today and you can  hear more from my conversation with  Sandberg on our CBS this morning podcast  find it on iTunes and Apple's podcast  app I went to a book party yesterday for  Sheryl Sandberg and nor you should know  everybody including Sheryl was  complimenting you about that interview  they thought you captured it brilliantly  I did too but she says it's a book that  she never planned or wanted to write  yeah and that now that it's here she  hopes it and I believe that it will help  a lot of people's self expression self  compassion and that it's okay to find  joy again Hart is it for her to revisit  so true Charlie you know we interview a  lot of people on this show you know this  is really one of the hardest interviews  I've ever done because it will talk to  someone about something so personal is  really I didn't realize she had found  him Nora I do I like that that's very  tough that's the one really do a really  good book you're right about that
 

